PHASE 2 – REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS

1. Introduction

Requirement analysis is the process of identifying what the FitBuddy application should do and what resources are required to develop it. The requirements are divided into functional and non-functional requirements.

2. Functional Requirements

The application should allow users to select their fitness goal, fitness level, and preferred number of workout days. After receiving these inputs, the system should process the information and display a suitable workout recommendation.

The application should provide different recommendations for goals such as weight loss, muscle gain, general fitness, and strength. It should also provide recommendations suitable for different fitness levels.

3. User Requirements

Users should be able to access the application easily through a web browser. The interface should provide clear options and buttons. Users should not require advanced technical knowledge to use the application.

4. Software Requirements

The project can be developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. A modern web browser such as Microsoft Edge, Google Chrome, or another compatible browser can be used to run the application.

5. Hardware Requirements

A computer, laptop, tablet, or smartphone with a web browser can be used to access the application. An internet connection may be required depending on the deployment method and future AI services.

6. Non-Functional Requirements

The application should be easy to use, responsive, reliable, and visually understandable. It should work properly on different screen sizes including mobile phones, tablets, and computers.

7. Security Requirements

If future versions include user accounts or personal information, suitable authentication and data protection mechanisms should be implemented. The application should avoid collecting unnecessary personal information.

8. Performance Requirements

The application should respond quickly when users select their preferences and generate a workout recommendation. The interface should remain smooth and usable on commonly available devices.

9. Requirement Summary

The requirement analysis provides a clear understanding of the features, resources, users, and technical requirements needed to develop the FitBuddy application.
